This project was created from ts-physics-template and hasn't run first-time setup yet.

Run `pnpm bootstrap`. It also runs automatically on `pnpm install` when you're at a
terminal. It asks who's working on this (solo/team), what you're building, the
project name, and the license — then wires everything up accordingly.

pnpm's builtin setup and init commands will not configure this project.

This file is deleted once setup completes. Until then, `pnpm verify` refuses to
pass, so setup can't be silently skipped. Deleting this file is not enough:
package.json name must also change off `ts-physics-template`.
